{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) issued a stitch task (Task ID: 5463) to implement `cmd/fmt` - a Go reimplementation of GNU `fmt` (text paragraph formatter). The task specifically targets srd070-fmt requirements R2.1 (blank line handling), R3.1 (indentation preservation), R4.1 (file/stdin input), and R5.1 (width control via `-w`/`--width`). Two files must be created: `cmd/fmt/main.go` (implementation) and `cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go` (differential tests against `gfmt` reference binary).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU `fmt` utility - paragraph reformatting to specified width (default 75 chars)\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against Homebrew `gfmt`\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - Graceful skip when reference binary not found (`exec.LookPath(\"gfmt\")` + `t.Skip`)\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for all differential tests\n   - SRD070-fmt full requirements: R1 (default 75-char formatting), R2 (blank lines as paragraph separators), R3 (indentation preservation), R4 (file/stdin input), R5 (width `-w`), R6 (goal width `-g`), R7 (word boundary breaking), R8 (space collapsing with sentence-end double spaces), R9 (split-only `-s`), R10 (uniform spacing `-u`), R11 (prefix mode `-p`), R12 (tagged-paragraph `-t`), R13 (exit codes + differential testing)\n   - Non-goals: crown margin mode (`-c`), locale-aware line breaking\n   - 40-line function size limit, 500-line file size limit\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd070-fmt.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SR