{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ANe9EjfzHiGSuisVmdgYYX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report of the patterns I found.\n\n## Go Unix Utils Project Patterns - Comprehensive Report\n\nBased on my analysis of the project, here are the key patterns used for implementing cmd/ utilities:\n\n---\n\n### **1. FLAG PARSING PATTERN**\n\nThe project uses **manual flag parsing** (not the standard `flag` package) to support Unix-style combined short flags.\n\n**Pattern in `cat/main.go`:**\n```go\nfunc parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n\tvar files []string\n\tendOfFlags := false\n\tfor _, arg := range args {\n\t\tif endOfFlags || arg == \"\" || arg == \"-\" || arg[0] != '-' {\n\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n\t\t\tendOfFlags = true\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, c := range arg[1:] {\n\t\t\tapplyFlag(c)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn files\n}\n\nfunc applyFlag(c rune) {\n\tswitch c {\n\tcase 'n':\n\t\tflagN = true\n\tcase 'b':\n\t\tflagB = true\n\t// ... etc\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n**Pattern in `wc/main.go` (more sophisticated):**\n- Separates short flags (`-l`, `-w`, `-c`) from long flags (`--lines`, `--words`)\n- Handles inline flag values (`-w5`) and separate values (`-w 5`)\n- Returns both options struct and remaining file arguments\n```go\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string) {\n\tvar opts options\n\tvar files []string\n\t// ... iterates through args, calls parseLongFlag or parseShortFlags\n}\n\nfunc parseLongFlag(arg string, _ []string, opts *options) (bool, int)\nfunc parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) int\n```\n\n**Pattern in `fold/main.go`:**\n- Uses `defaultOptions()` for option initialization\n- Returns `(options, []string, error)` for rich error handling during parsing\n```go\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (option, []string, error) {\n\topts := defaultOptions()\n\t// ... parsing with error return\n}\n```\n\n**Key characteristics:**\n- Global flag variables (cat) OR struct-based options (wc, fold)\n- Manual iteration to handle `-` and `--` \n- `endOfFlags` flag for `--` support\n- Error messages to stderr: `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"fold: %s\\n\", err)`\n\n---\n\n### **2. STDIN/FILE HANDLING PATTERN**\n\nAll utilities follow a consistent pattern:\n- Default to stdin (`-` or empty list) if no files provided\n- Support reading from stdin with `-` as explicit file argument\n- Handle both files and stdin transparently\n\n**Pattern from `cat/main.go`:**\n```go\nfunc main() {\n\targs := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n\tif len(args) == 0 {\n\t\targs = []string{\"-\"}  // Default to stdin\n\t}\n\t\n\tfor _, name := range args {\n\t\tlineNum, prevBlank, err = catFile(name, lineNum, prevBlank)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cat: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n\t\t\texitCode = 1\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc catFile(name string, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error) {\n\tvar r io.Reader\n\tif name == \"-\" {\n\t\tr = os.Stdin\n\t} else {\n\t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer f.Close()\n\t\tr = f\n\t}\n\t// ... process reader\n}\n```\n\n**Pattern from `wc/main.go`:**\n```go\nfunc countFile(name string) (counts, error) {\n\tvar r io.Reader\n\tif name == \"-\" || name == \"\" {\n\t\tr = os.Stdin\n\t} else {\n\t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn counts{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%s: %s\", name, err.(*os.PathError).Err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer f.Close()\n\t\tr = f\n\t}\n\treturn countReader(r)\n}\n```\n\n**Key characteristics:**\n- Use `io.Reader` interface for abstraction\n- Empty string (`\"\"`) and `\"-\"` both mean stdin\n- Proper error wrapping with filename context\n- Defer Close() for file cleanup\n\n---\n\n### **3. ERROR HANDLING PATTERN**\n\n**Exit codes:**\n- `0`: success\n- `1`: error occurred (file not found, invalid args, etc.)\n- Special: SIGPIPE errors exit `0` (not treated as failure)\n\n**Error reporting to stderr:**\n```go\nfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cat: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n```\n\n**SIGPIPE handling:**\n```go\nif errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n\tos.Exit(0)  // Exit cleanly when stdout closes\n}\n```\n\n**PathError formatting (from `cat/main.go`):**\n```go\nfunc formatErr(err error) string {\n\tvar pe *os.PathError\n\tif errors.As(err, &pe) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", pe.Path, pe.Err)\n\t}\n\treturn err.Error()\n}\n```\n\n**Partial failure pattern (from `wc/main.go`):**\n- Process all files even if some fail\n- Accumulate `hadError` flag\n- Return 1 if any error occurred\n```go\nfor _, f := range files {\n\tc, err := countFile(f)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, \"wc: %s\\n\", err)\n\t\thadError = true\n\t\tcontinue  // Continue with next file\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **4. SIGPIPE HANDLER PATTERN**\n\nAll utilities call this at the start of `main()`:\n\n**From `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n\tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n\tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n\tgo func() {\n\t\t<-c\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t}()\n}\n```\n\n**Usage in all utilities:**\n```go\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()  // Always first!\n\t// ... rest of logic\n}\n```\n\nThis allows graceful exit when piped to commands like `head` that close stdin early.\n\n---\n\n### **5. BUFFERED I/O PATTERN**\n\nFor streaming operations, utilities use `bufio.Reader` and `bufio.Writer`:\n\n**From `cat/main.go`:**\n```go\nfunc catTransform(r io.Reader, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error) {\n\tbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\n\tw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n\tfor {\n\t\tline, err := br.ReadBytes('\\n')\n\t\tif len(line) > 0 {\n\t\t\tlineNum, prevBlank = writeLine(w, line, lineNum, prevBlank)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tif err != io.EOF {\n\t\t\t\treadErr = err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif ferr := w.Flush(); ferr != nil {  // Always flush!\n\t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, ferr\n\t}\n\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, readErr\n}\n```\n\n**From `fold/main.go`:**\n```go\nw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\nexitCode := 0\nfor _, f := range files {\n\tif err := processFile(f, opts, w); err != nil {\n\t\t// ... error handling\n\t\texitCode = 1\n\t}\n}\nif err := w.Flush(); err != nil {\n\t// Handle flush errors (including SIGPIPE)\n\tif errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n**Key characteristics:**\n- Always flush before returning\n- Detect write errors during flush\n- Handle SIGPIPE during flush\n\n---\n\n### **6. DIFFERENTIAL TESTING PATTERN**\n\n**Test structure (from `cat_test.go` and `fold_test.go`):**\n\n```go\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")  // Compile the utility\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gcat\")     // Find GNU reference\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary gcat not found\")\n\t}\n\t\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{Name: \"default_stdin\", Stdin: []byte(\"hello\\nworld\\n\")},\n\t\t{Name: \"flag_n\", Args: []string{\"-n\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"alpha\\n\\nbeta\\n\")},\n\t\t{Name: \"combined_ns\", Args: []string{\"-n\", \"-s\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"a\\n\\n\\n\\nb\\n\")},\n\t\t// ... many more test cases\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n**DiffTest struct (from `pkg/testutils/difftest.go`):**\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string                  // Subtest name\n\tArgs          []string                // Command-line arguments\n\tStdin         []byte                  // Input (nil = EOF, []byte{} = open then close)\n\tEnv           []string                // Environment overrides (merged with inherited + LC_ALL=C)\n\tWorkDir       string                  // Working directory (defaults to t.TempDir())\n\tExitCode      int                     // Expected exit code (0 if zero value)\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc          // Output normalization functions\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte       // Files to verify after execution\n}\n```\n\n**RunDiffTests function:**\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tfor _, tc := range tests {\n\t\tt.Run(tc.Name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\trunSubtest(t, goBinary, refBinary, tc)\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Compiles the Go utility with `BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n2. Finds the GNU reference binary (e.g., `gcat`, `gfold`)\n3. For each test case:\n   - Runs both binaries with identical inputs\n   - Compares stdout, stderr, and exit code\n   - Applies normalizers (e.g., `TimestampNormalizer` for timestamp variations)\n   - Fails if outputs differ\n\n**Normalization pattern:**\n```go\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n\nvar TimestampNormalizer NormalizeFunc = func(b []byte) []byte {\n\t// Replace timestamp patterns with placeholder\n\tresult := b\n\tfor _, pat := range tsPatterns {\n\t\tresult = pat.ReplaceAll(result, []byte(\"<TIMESTAMP>\"))\n\t}\n\treturn result\n}\n\n// Usage:\nNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{\n\tdiscardStderr,\n\ttestutils.TimestampNormalizer,\n}\n```\n\n**Special test cases:**\n- **SIGPIPE test** (from `cat_test.go`):\n  ```go\n  func TestSIGPIPE(t *testing.T) {\n      // Creates large file, opens it, reads 1 byte, closes stdout\n      // Expects exit 0 (not timeout)\n      cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, goBin, largePath)\n      stdout, _ := cmd.StdoutPipe()\n      cmd.Start()\n      io.ReadFull(stdout, buf)\n      stdout.Close()  // Force SIGPIPE\n      err = cmd.Wait()\n      if err != nil {\n          t.Fatalf(\"expected exit 0 on SIGPIPE, got: %v\", err)\n      }\n  }\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### **7. OVERALL STRUCTURE PATTERN**\n\n**Main entry point:**\n```go\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\topts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n\texitCode := run(opts, files, os.Stdout, os.Stderr)\n\tos.Exit(exitCode)\n}\n\nfunc run(opts options, files []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n\tif len(files) == 0 {\n\t\tfiles = []string{\"-\"}  // Default stdin\n\t}\n\t// ... process files\n\treturn 0  // or 1 on error\n}\n```\n\nThis pattern:\n- Installs SIGPIPE handler first\n- Uses dependency injection for stdout/stderr (testable)\n- Returns exit code from `run()` and exits with it\n- Separates parsing from execution\n\n---\n\n### **Key Files Reference:**\n\n- **Flag parsing**: `/cmd/cat/main.go` (simple), `/cmd/wc/main.go` (complex), `/cmd/fold/main.go` (with errors)\n- **SIGPIPE handler**: `/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n- **Diff testing**: `/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`, `/pkg/testutils/build.go`\n- **Test examples**: `/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`, `/cmd/fold/fold_test.go`\n\nThe project demonstrates a mature Unix utilities implementation with consistent patterns for portability, testability, and correct error handling."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ad3de8b-52b6-448c-b359-efd0ade26f4f","uuid":"4282b2c1-d0e2-4937-84dc-c88637e6cef9","timestamp":"2026-05-22T19:25:04.265Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand patterns used in this Go project for implementing cmd/ utilities. Look at:\n\n1. A few existing cmd/*/main.go files to understand the flag parsing pattern, error handling, and overall structure. Pick 2-3 that exist and seem representative (e.g., cmd/cat/main.go, cmd/fold/main.go, cmd/wc/main.go, or similar text-processing utilities).\n\n2. Read pkg/sys/sigpipe.go to see InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n3. Read pkg/testutils/difftest.go to understand DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function signature\n\n4. Read a few cmd/*/XXX_test.go files to see the differential testing pattern (pick 2 that exist)\n\nReport back the key patterns: how flags are parsed, how stdin/files are handled, how errors are reported, how tests are structured. Include relevant code snippets.","agentId":"af2b949acb7bb0d03","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report of the patterns I found.\n\n## Go Unix Utils Project Patterns - Comprehensive Report\n\nBased on my analysis of the project, here are the key patterns used for implementing cmd/ utilities:\n\n---\n\n### **1. FLAG PARSING PATTERN**\n\nThe project uses **manual flag parsing** (not the standard `flag` package) to support Unix-style combined short flags.\n\n**Pattern in `cat/main.go`:**\n```go\nfunc parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n\tvar files []string\n\tendOfFlags := false\n\tfor _, arg := range args {\n\t\tif endOfFlags || arg == \"\" || arg == \"-\" || arg[0] != '-' {\n\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n\t\t\tendOfFlags = true\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, c := range arg[1:] {\n\t\t\tapplyFlag(c)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn files\n}\n\nfunc applyFlag(c rune) {\n\tswitch c {\n\tcase 'n':\n\t\tflagN = true\n\tcase 'b':\n\t\tflagB = true\n\t// ... etc\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n**Pattern in `wc/main.go` (more sophisticated):**\n- Separates short flags (`-l`, `-w`, `-c`) from long flags (`--lines`, `--words`)\n- Handles inline flag values (`-w5`) and separate values (`-w 5`)\n- Returns both options struct and remaining file arguments\n```go\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string) {\n\tvar opts options\n\tvar files []string\n\t// ... iterates through args, calls parseLongFlag or parseShortFlags\n}\n\nfunc parseLongFlag(arg string, _ []string, opts *options) (bool, int)\nfunc parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) int\n```\n\n**Pattern in `fold/main.go`:**\n- Uses `defaultOptions()` for option initialization\n- Returns `(options, []string, error)` for rich error handling during parsing\n```go\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (option, []string, error) {\n\topts := defaultOptions()\n\t// ... parsing with error return\n}\n```\n\n**Key characteristics:**\n- Global flag variables (cat) OR struct-based options (wc, fold)\n- Manual iteration to handle `-` and `--` \n- `endOfFlags` flag for `--` support\n- Error messages to stderr: `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"fold: %s\\n\", err)`\n\n---\n\n### **2. STDIN/FILE HANDLING PATTERN**\n\nAll utilities follow a consistent pattern:\n- Default to stdin (`-` or empty list) if no files provided\n- Support reading from stdin with `-` as explicit file argument\n- Handle both files and stdin transparently\n\n**Pattern from `cat/main.go`:**\n```go\nfunc main() {\n\targs := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n\tif len(args) == 0 {\n\t\targs = []string{\"-\"}  // Default to stdin\n\t}\n\t\n\tfor _, name := range args {\n\t\tlineNum, prevBlank, err = catFile(name, lineNum, prevBlank)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cat: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n\t\t\texitCode = 1\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc catFile(name string, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error) {\n\tvar r io.Reader\n\tif name == \"-\" {\n\t\tr = os.Stdin\n\t} else {\n\t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer f.Close()\n\t\tr = f\n\t}\n\t// ... process reader\n}\n```\n\n**Pattern from `wc/main.go`:**\n```go\nfunc countFile(name string) (counts, error) {\n\tvar r io.Reader\n\tif name == \"-\" || name == \"\" {\n\t\tr = os.Stdin\n\t} else {\n\t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn counts{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%s: %s\", name, err.(*os.PathError).Err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer f.Close()\n\t\tr = f\n\t}\n\treturn countReader(r)\n}\n```\n\n**Key characteristics:**\n- Use `io.Reader` interface for abstraction\n- Empty string (`\"\"`) and `\"-\"` both mean stdin\n- Proper error wrapping with filename context\n- Defer Close() for file cleanup\n\n---\n\n### **3. ERROR HANDLING PATTERN**\n\n**Exit codes:**\n- `0`: success\n- `1`: error occurred (file not found, invalid args, etc.)\n- Special: SIGPIPE errors exit `0` (not treated as failure)\n\n**Error reporting to stderr:**\n```go\nfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cat: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n```\n\n**SIGPIPE handling:**\n```go\nif errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n\tos.Exit(0)  // Ex